course: dictionary
lesson: 6692
title: How often? Words of frequency
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how often something happens. «Occasionally» means sometimes, but not often or regularly. If you occasionally have pizza, it happens now and then, not every week.
explain: Frequency words sit on a scale: never, rarely, occasionally, sometimes, often, usually, always. Occasionally is near the rare end, so it is more than rarely but less than often. Look at the words around it, such as often, every day or never, to see where it fits.
explain: Context gives you the clue. «Rickets is a bone disease caused by lack of vitamin D, making bones soft and legs bowed; it was common in smoky cities and is still occasionally seen.» The word «still» tells you rickets is not common now, but it does still turn up now and then. Occasionally means not often.
fact: Occasionally means sometimes, but not often or regularly.
fact: Frequency words show how often something happens: never, rarely, occasionally, sometimes, often, usually, always.
fact: «We occasionally have pizza» means we have pizza now and then.
fact: «Only occasionally» and «very occasionally» are common phrases; «very occasionally» means even less often.
fact: «Occasionally» is an adverb: it tells you how often something happens.
exercise: «We occasionally have pizza.» What does occasionally mean? | Every day | Very quickly | Never at all | *Now and then
exercise: Mum says, «I occasionally visit Grandma.» How often does Mum visit? | Every week, on the same day | Every single day | Never | *Now and then, not on a regular plan
exercise: On the scale never, rarely, occasionally, sometimes, often, usually, always, which word comes straight after rarely? | Usually | *Occasionally | Always | Never
test: «Rickets is still occasionally seen.» What does this tell you? | *It is seen now and then, not all the time | It is seen every day in every city | It has never been seen again | It is seen only in smoky cities, always
test: Which sentence shows something happening now and then? | *Ella occasionally walks to school with her dad. | Ella walks to school at exactly eight o'clock each day. | Ella never walks to school at all. | Ella always walks to school in the rain.
exam: Jayden says occasionally means always. Is he right? | *No, it means now and then, not often | Yes, it means only in the morning | Yes, it means every time, without fail | No, it means never at all
